# W44-AUDIT-6 Phase 2A — W44-109 win-cluster regression validation

**Date:** 2026-05-24
**Status:** [SHIPPED — gates a/b/c/d/e PASS]
**Parent commit:** post-`3eb09c6f` (AUDIT-6 Phase 1 SHIPPED)
**TSV:** `benchmarks/w44_audit_6_phase2a_win_cluster_2026-05-24.tsv`
**Reproducer:** `cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release \
                  --features "parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop __expert" \
                  --example w44_audit_6_phase2a_win_cluster`
**Wall time:** 97.4 s (15 cells × 4 encodes/cell = 60 encodes + scoring)

## Hypothesis (per Phase 1 brief)

W44-AUDIT-6 Phase 1 added a `m3_colourfulness >= 80.0` sub-discriminator
to the W44-109 lift gate. The W44-109 win cluster (text-class
screenshots: terminal/imac_g3/imac_dark/graph/gmessages at e ∈ {5, 6, 7}
× d ∈ {3, 4}) has M3 ∈ [10, 29] ≪ 80.0; the AUDIT-6 discriminator
should therefore NOT fire on any of these cells. Production B mode
(AUDIT-6 ON by default) MUST produce **byte-identical** output to mode
A (`JXL_W44_AUDIT_6_DISABLE=1`) on every win-cluster cell.

