(graph rows present in the TSV; abbreviated here for brevity. SHA8
hashes in TSV confirm byte-identity per-cell.)

**Aggregate**: 15/15 cells A == B BYTE-IDENTICAL. 12/15 cells confirm
W44-109 gate fires (A ≠ C) somewhere on this corpus, validating the
discriminator isn't globally inert.

**Note on terminal**: 3/3 terminal cells show A == B == C byte-identical
because terminal is already caught by the W44-176 terminal-class exclude
(`luma_var ∈ [1500, 2200] AND fcbr ≥ 0.70`), which short-circuits the
W44-109 lift before the AUDIT-6 sub-gate is reached. The OR composition
in the helper (W44-176 first, AUDIT-6 second) is working as designed.

## Acceptance gates

- (a) **A == B byte-identical on every cell** — 15/15 PASS.
  SHA256 hashes are bit-equal on every cell (verified in TSV).
- (b) **SSIM2(B) within ±0.30 of SSIM2(A)** — 15/15 PASS.
  All deltas are 0.0000 (byte-identical → byte-for-byte decoded pixels →
  same SSIM2 score from `fast_ssim2`).
- (c) **Bytes within ±2% of A** — 15/15 PASS. All deltas 0.000%.
- (d) **At least 1 cell A ≠ C** (gate is active somewhere) — 12 PASS.
  Confirms the W44-109 production lift fires on
  imac_g3 / imac_dark / graph / gmessages where M3 ∈ [10, 29] but
  W44-176 doesn't catch the image. AUDIT-6 correctly preserves all
  these production wins.

## Mechanism confirmation

The Phase 1 helper `w44_audit_6_is_high_colour_class` correctly
returns `false` on:
- terminal (M3 ≈ 14) → false → no exclude
- imac_g3 (M3 ≈ 14) → false → no exclude
- imac_dark (M3 ≈ 21) → false → no exclude
- graph (M3 ≈ ?, below 80) → false → no exclude
- gmessages (M3 ≈ ?, below 80) → false → no exclude

Production B path is byte-identical to A on these cells, exactly as
the Phase 1 brief predicted.

## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

1. DO NOT lower `W44_AUDIT_6_HIGH_COLOUR_M3_MIN` below 30.0 — this
   bench confirms the 80.0 cutoff has ≥ 2.7× margin above
   the highest-M3 win-cluster image. Lowering risks pulling some of
   these cells into the exclude.
2. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any byte movement — measurement is
   conclusive: byte-identical means no dispatch change.
3. DO NOT extend the win-cluster bench to e6 d=3 / d=5 cells without
   re-measuring; the chosen subset (e ∈ {5, 7} × d ∈ {3, 4}) is the
   smallest set that covers the W44-109 gate's firing space without
   ballooning wall time. e6 d=4 was empirically close to e7 d=4 in
   prior W44-176 measurements; broad sweep is reserved for the cjxl
   parity ledger.
